    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16176" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">errātĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				wandering</i>, <i>roving about.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hac multo propius ibis et minor est erratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Ad. 4, 2, 41</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 1, 2, 90</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				2, 21, 56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Univ.
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in factis dictisque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 5, 17, 29</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Astr. 2, 2</span></i>.</div>
